.TH _TERMFP 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
_termfp \- terminal-based file picker wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B _termfp
\fIMODE_MULTIPLE\fR \fIMODE_DIR\fR \fIMODE_SAVE\fR \fISTART_PATH\fR \fISAVE_PATH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B _termfp
is a wrapper script that provides a terminal-based file and directory chooser.
It executes an interactive bash shell within a new
.BR kitty (1)
window, which is spawned with the class "termfp" and title "Terminal File Picker".
.PP
Inside this shell environment, a custom
.B yield
command is injected to process the user's selection.
The script handles path validation based on the supplied execution modes and writes the absolute paths to a save file.
If no valid paths are provided or if the selection rules are broken, the script clears the save file and returns an error.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B MODE_MULTIPLE
Set to 1 to allow multiple selections, or 0 to restrict to a single selection.
.TP
.B MODE_DIR
Set to 1 to require the selected target to be a directory, or 0 for files.
.TP
.B MODE_SAVE
Set to 1 for "Save" mode, which resolves absolute paths even if the file does not yet exist.
.TP
.B START_PATH
The initial path for the file picker.
.TP
.B SAVE_PATH
The destination file path where the 
.B yield
command will write the chosen absolute paths.
.SH THE YIELD COMMAND
The injected
.B yield
command is used to confirm selections inside the shell.
It accepts targets either as positional arguments or through piped input.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. The save file contains valid selected data.
.TP
.B 1
Failure or cancellation. The save file is empty or invalid selections were made.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR kitty (1)
